The policy on licenses has changed so often that I lost track. As a
general rule of thumb, layered products PAKs may be transferred to
other systems belonging to the same owner. IIRC there's no need to
inform HP that a product has been moved, provided that the PAK is used
just on one system and for the amount of units it was issued for The
units in use may be less, but definitely not more. The MOD_UNITS
option present on most layered products PAK's was intended to ease
migration and because DEC's own administration was not accurate nor
fast when the PAK's were introduced.
OS licenses were tied to specific hardware but migration was offered
as a service by DEC and Compaq. No idea how HP handles this.
Transferring equipment and licenses to other parties was possible,
again no idea what HP's current policy is.
This applies for company owned systems. Hobbyist systems tend to use
the Montagar hobbyist PAK's but if you transfer the PAK's to
intereseted hobbyists I think HP wouldn't mind and even if they
officially would mind I guess they can't be bothered. It seems that
even new paying VMS customers are hardly noticed at all when shopping
let alone older products from DEC :-(
Hans

PS
You're not in Europe, are you?


